  return const KkBlink(child: SizedBox(width: 10, height: 10));
}), motion: true);
// then 14 x tester.pump(100 ms), collecting tester.widget<Opacity>(find.byType(Opacity)).opacity

Output:
reduceMotion: MediaQuery.reduceMotion=true motionOf=true opacities over 1.4s={1.0, 0.2}
  Expected: false
    Actual: <true>
  the platform asked for reduced motion
Control with FakeAccessibilityFeatures(disableAnimations: true) passes:
disableAnimations: motionOf=false opacities over 1.4s={1.0}

SDK documentation on disk, /opt/sdk/flutter/packages/flutter/lib/src/widgets/media_query.dart (Flutter 3.50.1), MediaQueryData.disableAnimations: "This corresponds to Android's \"Remove animations\" accessibility setting. On iOS, reduced motion is exposed separately via [dart:ui.AccessibilityFeatures.reduceMotion] and does not set this flag." and MediaQueryData.reduceMotion: "This corresponds to the iOS \"Reduce Motion\" accessibility setting."

suggestedFix:
static bool motionOf(BuildContext context) {
  if (!of(context).motion.enabled) return false;
  if (MediaQuery.maybeDisableAnimationsOf(context) ?? false) return false;
  return !(MediaQuery.maybeReduceMotionOf(context) ?? false);
}
MediaQuery.maybeReduceMotionOf exists in the pinned SDK (media_query.dart:2073); raise the `flutter: ">=3.35.0"` lower bound in pubspec.yaml if that API is newer than 3.35. Add a test with FakeAccessibilityFeatures(reduceMotion: true).

